false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.6.stable.official [89cea1439]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.stable - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4060 Laptop GPU (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8097) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-14900HX (32 threads) - 31.62 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/be558378-5a1c-4bca-be90-9fea78c54361\n\nThe Theme Editor has strange behavior, which does not occur in the running game. For example these buttons are shrinking (after a random time hovered) and remain shrunk (again for a random time) after unhovering. \n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nSee MRP. The setup is a few buttons in an HBoxContainer, where the scene has a theme with a single value set: The `hover` field of `Button` with a default/new `StyleBoxFlat`\n\nYou can open `theme.tres` and then add `example.tscn` as a custom preview. Hover the buttons to see the odd behavior. \n\nYou can also run `example.tscn` to compare.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[buttonstyleboxmrp_2026-04-06_22-08-31.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/26519893/buttonstyleboxmrp_2026-04-06_22-08-31.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}